  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` now passes with 6 of 6 tests.\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a job that rejected or threw never decremented `running`, so the queue stalled. Jobs are now wrapped so that a sync throw, a rejection or a plain return value all settle that job's own promise. The queue then frees the slot and moves on.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending, so it could resolve while jobs were still running. It now also requires `running === 0`.\n- **One job at a time after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until the free slots are full or the queue is empty.\n\nI added four regression tests in `test/queue.test.js`:\n- Failure recovery, covering a sync throw and an async rejection followed by a good job.\n- Plain-value jobs.\n- `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs.\n- `resume()` filling all four slots, checking that exactly four jobs run at once.\n\nI haven't run the new tests against the old code to confirm they fail there.",
